# Cascade — Debug and automation surface

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
Cascade carries a debugging and automation surface, `window.__cascade`, so the
game can be driven and inspected from code without moving a real pointer or
waiting on real time.

You implement it. Every operation this file specifies is a deliverable, and the
build installs the finished surface on `window.__cascade` as soon as the game has
initialized. Every scenario driven from code reaches the game through it, so it
is present and exactly as specified here.

Each operation is a read of the game's state, a pose of one field of it, a move
of the clock, one of the game's own events, or one of the game's own draws. A
pose arranges the table, and the game's own move rules, turning, win test, and
cascade run from there exactly as they do in play, so a scenario driven from
code behaves exactly like one played by hand.

The surface is inert during normal play, doing nothing until something calls it.
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
